---
import FullBleedHero from "./FullBleedHero.astro";
import FullBleedBreak from "./FullBleedBreak.astro";
import { withBase } from "../lib/url";
---

<FullBleedHero title="Community" image="/hero/community.jpg" imageAlt="An electric bus charging at a depot in Kenya">
  <p class="text-lg text-text">
    AfCA convenes Charge Point Operators, Electromobility Service Providers, electric utilities,
    fleet operators, hardware OEMs, and policymakers around shared, published standards — not
    closed-door advisory relationships with individual companies.
  </p>
</FullBleedHero>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-content px-6 py-10 md:py-16">
  <h2 class="font-sans text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Membership</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-prose text-text-muted">
    {/* TODO: membership tiers, fees, and eligibility criteria — pending governance sign-off. */}
    Membership tiers, fees, and eligibility criteria are being finalised alongside AfCA's Rwanda
    registration and will be published here once confirmed. Participation follows the open-call
    principle described in the <a href={withBase("/about")} class="text-ink underline">operating principles</a>:
    organisations self-select against published criteria rather than being hand-picked.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-14 font-sans text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Working groups</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-prose text-text-muted">
    {/* TODO: list active working groups once formally constituted. */}
    Working groups are formed around specific technical or policy questions — interoperability
    testing, tariff harmonisation, or a country's regulatory framework, for example — and publish
    their outputs openly rather than as member-only deliverables. The initial slate of working
    groups will be announced alongside the first AfCA Summit.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-14 font-sans text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Participant directory</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-prose text-text-muted">
    {/* TODO: populate with confirmed participants. No customer-showcase framing — factual data points only, per BRIEF.md section 8. */}
    A directory of confirmed participating organisations will appear here. In keeping with AfCA's
    vendor-neutral positioning, this will list organisations as factual participants — not as
    testimonials or an implied endorsement.
  </p>

  <FullBleedBreak image="/hero/summit.jpg" imageAlt="Nairobi skyline at dusk" caption="Nairobi at dusk" />

  <h2 id="summit" class="scroll-mt-24 font-sans text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">The AfCA Annual Summit</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-prose text-lg text-text">
    Curated representation across the value chain, action-oriented workshops rather than panels,
    and a catalyst for regional initiatives, donor-funded corridor pilots, and harmonised policy
    recommendations.
  </p>

  <h3 class="mt-10 font-sans text-xl font-semibold text-ink">What the Summit is for</h3>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-prose text-text">
    The Summit exists to produce outcomes, not to be attended. Every session is built around a
    working deliverable — a draft standard, a corridor pilot proposal, a policy recommendation —
    rather than a stage and an audience.
  </p>

  <h3 class="mt-10 font-sans text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Dates and location</h3>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-prose text-text-muted">
    {/* TODO: confirm dates, city, and venue once finalised. */}
    Dates and location for the first AfCA Summit will be announced here once confirmed.
  </p>

  <h3 class="mt-10 font-sans text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Participation</h3>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-prose text-text-muted">
    {/* TODO: registration process and criteria. */}
    Representation is curated across the value chain rather than open registration, consistent
    with AfCA's open-call principle: organisations apply against published criteria. Details on
    how to apply will be published ahead of the first Summit.
  </p>
</section>
